From d94c6442d3d1e53f5ff72d22ed188889ce681d51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:02:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: add a diagnostic for everything after the audio pump in
 the loop

Per-fix real-hardware gains have been shrinking (blit-rect-limiting
+52%, present-rect-limiting +26%, worldX-hoist +14%, HashTable-bitmask
+4.7%), and after patches 0015/0016 the render loop no longer has an
obvious next hoist-style bug -- its remaining ~46ms is spread across
several smaller things (cache-miss-only chest/noise checks, the
inherent cost of sampling twice per pixel) with no single dominant
culprit found by re-reading it further. Rather than keep guessing
inside the render loop, this instruments a part of the frame that has
never been measured at all: everything from "start timing next frame"
(after the SDL_Delay pacing call) to the end of the while loop body --
input handling via getKeyDown() (which calls SDL_PumpEvents() roughly
ten times per frame, once per key checked), movement, stepAnimations(),
the SDL_PollEvent quit-check loop, and chest/spouse/score bookkeeping.

Running tally going into this: render loop ~46ms (patches 0015/0016) +
flip (blowup+blit+present) ~56ms (patches 0012-0014) + audio pump
~20-25ms (patches 0007/0008) = ~125ms against a real ~145ms average
frame time (486DX2-50, patch 0016's confirmation round) -- only ~20ms
of slack expected here, so this section is not expected to dominate.
Given this investigation's track record (the last several "not expected
to dominate" guesses were each wrong at least once before being ruled
out with real data), measuring directly rather than assuming is still
the right call.

Adds `LOGICDBG.LOG` (`__DJGPP__`-guarded, temporary, same 20-frame-
window pattern as the other three diagnostics in this series): times
the whole span, logs `[rest-of-loop-cost n=20] avg_ms=...`. No behavior
change -- purely additive timing around code that's otherwise
untouched.

Verified under DOSBox-X: builds, boots, plays normally, LOGICDBG.LOG
populates (avg_ms 3.0-5.5 on this host -- small, as the ~20ms-of-slack
estimate above would suggest, though DOSBox-X magnitude has never been
authoritative in this investigation). Clean boot/play/ESCAPE-quit, no
hang. Real-hardware measurement on the 486DX2-50 is the next step, to
see whether this section holds to the ~20ms slack estimate or turns out
to be another underestimated cost.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index f2459d9..7db0c44 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -1315,7 +1315,24 @@ char playGame() {
 
         // start timing next frame
         lastFrameTimeStamp = Time::getCurrentTime();
-        
+
+
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        // TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC (LOGICDBG.LOG): the render loop
+        // (RENDERDBG.LOG), the present path (FLIPDBG.LOG), and the audio
+        // pump (PUMPDBG.LOG) are all individually timed elsewhere in this
+        // loop -- but everything from here to the end of the loop body
+        // (input handling via getKeyDown(), which calls SDL_PumpEvents()
+        // roughly ten times per frame; movement; stepAnimations(); the
+        // SDL_PollEvent quit-check loop; chest/spouse/score bookkeeping)
+        // has never been measured. Real-hardware data (486DX2-50) put
+        // render loop (~46ms after patches 0015/0016) + flip (~56ms,
+        // patches 0013/0014) + pump (~20-25ms) at roughly ~125ms against
+        // a real ~145ms frame time -- only ~20ms of slack, so this
+        // section is not expected to dominate, but "not expected to" has
+        // been wrong more than once already in this investigation.
+        double restOfLoopStartTime = Time::getCurrentTime();
+#endif
 
 
         int spouseX, spouseY;
@@ -1641,10 +1658,33 @@ char playGame() {
         if( exploreScore > maxExploreScore ) {
             maxExploreScore = exploreScore;
             }
-            
-        
+
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        {
+            double restOfLoopElapsed =
+                Time::getCurrentTime() - restOfLoopStartTime;
+            static double restOfLoopElapsedTotal = 0;
+            static int restOfLoopFrameCount = 0;
+            restOfLoopElapsedTotal += restOfLoopElapsed;
+            restOfLoopFrameCount ++;
+            if( restOfLoopFrameCount >= 20 ) {
+                FILE *logicLog = fopen( "LOGICDBG.LOG", "a" );
+                if( logicLog != NULL ) {
+                    fprintf( logicLog,
+                             "[rest-of-loop-cost n=%d] avg_ms=%f\n",
+                             restOfLoopFrameCount,
+                             1000.0 * restOfLoopElapsedTotal /
+                                 restOfLoopFrameCount );
+                    fclose( logicLog );
+                    }
+                restOfLoopElapsedTotal = 0;
+                restOfLoopFrameCount = 0;
+                }
+            }
+#endif
+
         }
-    
+
     unsigned long netTime = time( NULL ) - startTime;
     double frameRate = frameCount / (double)netTime;
     
